  "final_answer": "I have found the information needed. Let me provide a clear summary.\n\n## Answer\n\n**Latest Pre-trained Language Model Suitable for Text Classification on Hugging Face**\n\nThe latest model in the **Text Classification** filter (sorted by \"Recently updated\") on Hugging Face is:\n\n### **`orpe42/deberta_MP_dynamic`**\n- **URL**: https://huggingface.co/orpe42/deberta_MP_dynamic\n- **Updated**: Less than a minute ago (most recently updated as of today)\n- **License**: MIT\n- **Model size**: ~0.4B parameters\n- **Tags**: Transformers, TensorBoard, Safetensors, Generated from Trainer, text-embeddings-inference, deberta-v2\n\n### Intended Use Case\nThe model is a **fine-tuned version of `microsoft/deberta-v3-large`** intended for **text classification** tasks. Based on the reported evaluation metrics (Macro F1: 0.5491, Micro F1: 0.6332, Macro Roc Auc: 0.9217, Exact Match Ratio: 0.0853), it appears to be designed for multi-class or multi-label text classification tasks where distinguishing between multiple text categories is the goal. The high ROC AUC (~0.92) indicates strong class separability, while the lower Exact Match Ratio suggests it may also handle tasks with many possible labels (e.g., large-label classification).\n\n### Architecture\nThe architecture is based on **DeBERTa (Decoding-enhanced BERT with Disentangled Attention), specifically the v3-large variant from Microsoft**. Key architectural features of DeBERTa include:\n- **Disentangled attention mechanism**: Uses separate vectors for content and relative position, rather than mixing them.\n- **Enhanced mask decoder**: Incorporates absolute positions in the decoding layer to better predict masked tokens.\n- **Electra-style pre-training (v3)**: Replaces the masked language modeling objective with replaced token detection for more efficient pre-training.\n- **Large variant**: ~435M parameters, using 24 layers with a hidden size of 1024.\n\nThe underlying pre-trained foundation model (`microsoft/deberta-v3-large`) is a state-of-the-art transformer-based language model that excels at a wide variety of natural language understanding tasks, including text classification, and is itself widely used as a base model for downstream fine-tuning.",
